      "edu.eyebrow": "Learn: the five attachment patterns",
      "edu.teaser":
        "Secure, anxious, avoidant, disorganized, contextual: five ways a nervous system learns to hold closeness. Most couples are living a combination of two, and knowing both changes how every conflict between you reads.",
      "edu.body.p1":
        "Attachment style is how your system handles closeness, dependence, reassurance, and distance in intimacy. It isn't neediness, independence, or maturity, and it isn't a verdict on your character. It's what your nervous system learned about whether closeness is safe, and desire organizes itself around that learning. It also shapes what sex is quietly doing: serving as reassurance, bonding, escape, or regulation.",
