        '3. When restlessness rises, say it instead of acting on it: "I\'m bored, not gone. Throw me something new." Restlessness said out loud becomes play. Restlessness kept hidden becomes distance.',
      "body.p1":
        "Your nervous system watches for one thing: being trapped. Monotony, monitoring, sex that starts to feel like an obligation: it registers these early, long before you consciously feel bored, which is why wanting can vanish while nothing seems wrong. People who call that commitment-phobia are misreading a smoke detector as arson. The alarm is information. Answer what set it off, out loud, and it stops running the show.",
