      "gate.hook": "You didn't choose your beliefs about sex. A few quietly box you in.",
      "edu.eyebrow": "Learn: where beliefs come from",
      "edu.teaser":
        "Most sexual beliefs were installed before you had any say: by family silence, religion, culture, and first experiences. They now run as automatic filters on which desires are allowed to surface at all.",
      "edu.body.p1":
        "Sexual beliefs form early and mostly without words: what was never mentioned at home, what carried shame, what first experiences were rewarded or punished. By adulthood they operate as automatic filters, deciding which desires feel legitimate, which feel dangerous, and which never reach consciousness at all.",
      "edu.body.p2":
        "A handful of belief clusters show up again and again. None is right or wrong:\n• Pleasure and outcome: sex is about enjoyment, release, novelty.\n• Validation and approval: being wanted proves worth.\n• Power and control: sex sets safety or hierarchy.\n• Relational and bonding: sex creates closeness and reassurance.\n• Service and other: sex is about pleasing the partner and keeping harmony.\n• Exploration and growth: sex is a place to learn and expand.\n• Stability and safety: sex belongs to routine and commitment.\n• Avoidant or defensive: sex feels risky, so it stays distant or minimized.\nEach began as an adaptive response to an early environment. Trouble starts only when a belief goes rigid, stays unconscious, or clashes with a partner's.",
      "body.p1":
        "Yours mostly formed where love arrived for being helpful, and asking for things felt like the fastest way to lose it. None of them are wrong. Held too tightly, they put your own wants last so reliably that you stop feeling them, and a want you cannot feel cannot be met.",
