      "edu.eyebrow": "Learn: bids and repair",
      "edu.teaser":
        "Relationships don't fail on conflict. They fail on unanswered bids for connection. Couples that last don't fight less; they turn toward each other's bids more often, and they repair faster after missing one.",
      "edu.body.p1":
        'Relationship research calls small reaches for connection bids: a comment, a touch, an "I miss us." Couples that last don\'t bid less or fight less; they turn toward bids more often, and they repair faster after missing one.',
      "edu.body.p2":
        "Loops like this one form when bids arrive in a dialect the partner mishears (depth-bids heard as criticism, play-bids heard as pressure). Translating the bid, saying what it's actually asking for in doable terms, is the single most valuable repair skill a couple can learn.",
      "edu.body.p3":
        'Make the bid doable. "This feels disconnected" becomes "ten minutes together tonight, phones away." "It feels routine" becomes "new place this weekend, you pick." A request with a size beats a request with a mood.',
