      "edu.eyebrow": "Learn: the five attachment patterns",
      "edu.teaser":
        "Secure, anxious, avoidant, disorganized, contextual: five ways a nervous system learns to hold closeness. Most couples are living a combination of two, and knowing both changes how every conflict between you reads.",
      "edu.body.p1":
        "Attachment style is how your system handles closeness, dependence, reassurance, and distance in intimacy. It isn't neediness, independence, or maturity, and it isn't a verdict on your character. It's what your nervous system learned about whether closeness is safe, and desire organizes itself around that learning. It also shapes what sex is quietly doing: serving as reassurance, bonding, escape, or regulation.",
      "edu.body.p2":
        "Secure: closeness and autonomy both feel safe; desire stays stable across phases.",
      "edu.body.p3":
        "Anxious: highly attuned to signs of closeness or rejection; desire intertwines with reassurance.",
      "edu.body.p4":
        "Avoidant: values autonomy and self-containment; closeness can feel engulfing, and novelty feels safer than sustained intimacy.",
      "edu.body.p5":
        "Disorganized / mixed: closeness is both wanted and threatening; desire surges and collapses unpredictably.",
      "edu.body.p6":
        "Contextual: attachment expression shifts with partner, power dynamics, and safety.",
      "body.p1":
        "Start with the solid dot: your everyday base, open, collaborative, close without losing yourself. The glow around it shows how much of the map already feels like home. The hollow dot is where feeling judged sends you: still secure underneath, but now checking for approval, reading feedback as rejection, going quiet to avoid a mistake. Watch which way it drifts. It moves toward worry, not away from your partner. Kind encouragement, repeated across ordinary moments, is what settles the dot back home.",
      "edu.body.p7":
        "Attachment isn't static. It softens or hardens across life stages, relationships, and repair experiences.",
      "learn.eyebrow": "What you will learn",
      "learn.body":
        "In this chapter you will learn what attachment is and how it shapes closeness during sex. Why you open up or pull back with a partner, and what quietly moves you between the two.",
