      "practical.line3":
        '3. Close a false alarm out loud: "That felt messy for a second. Are we still good?" Said plainly, one unclear moment stops turning into a shutdown.',
      "body.p1":
        "You read one signal before all others: is the frame respected and clear. The instant a moment turns disrespectful, chaotic, or vague, something in you closes desire down to keep you safe. It fires early, often before the anger even reaches you, which is why wanting can vanish while nothing looks obviously wrong. This is a detector, not a defect. It catches instability most people walk straight past. The fix is never wanting less control. It's a frame agreed out loud, and a partner who honors it instead of testing it.",
