      "edu.eyebrow": "Learn: pleasure's preconditions",
      "edu.teaser":
        "Enjoyment problems are rarely about sex itself. They're about what the body needs settled before pleasure is allowed. Which precondition matters most differs by profile, and pushing through unmet ones makes the next time harder.",
      "edu.body.p1":
        "Difficulty enjoying sex is usually a precondition problem: the nervous system needs certain things settled first (safety, alignment, non-distraction, self-permission), and which ones matter most differs by profile. Pushing through unmet preconditions teaches the body that sex means override, which makes the next time harder.",
      "edu.body.p2":
        'It also helps to know your desire may be responsive rather than spontaneous: it emerges after the conditions are met, not before, so waiting to "feel like it" first can keep you waiting. And when desire shuts down, that\'s usually self-protection, not rejection of your partner. The system is holding desire back until it trusts the conditions are right.',
